The <symplectic neighborhood theorem> says that a neighborhood of a compact <symplectic submanifold> is determined, up to symplectomorphism, by the restricted symplectic form and its <symplectic normal bundle>. More precisely, if $f:S_0\to S_1$ is a symplectomorphism and an isomorphism of symplectic normal bundles covers $f$, then that bundle isomorphism extends to a symplectomorphism between neighborhoods of $S_0$ and $S_1$.

